        "problem": "If $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ then what is $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}?$",
        "worked_solution": "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-4)+(-5)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2+12-12-30 \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
